{:edb/db-before-t 2720 :edb/db-after-t 2721 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536033 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:19:17.720Z" 13194139536033 true] [17592186119754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380192 13194139536033 true] [17592186119754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380199 13194139536033 true] [17592186119755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380206 13194139536033 true] [17592186119755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380213 13194139536033 true] [17592186119755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380220 13194139536033 true] [17592186380192 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380193 13194139536033 true] [17592186380192 1089 "q-127873" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380192 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536033 true] [17592186380192 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380192 1113 #uuid "401ba6bc-fa27-5ba0-acab-8c53d45558b9" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380192 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380194 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380195 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380196 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380197 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380198 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1041 "selection" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380196 13194139536033 true] [17592186380193 1110 #uuid "51cbf961-880f-5565-ab09-ae794ec61fcf" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380194 1034 "3" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380194 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380194 1111 #uuid "49147c48-3c79-59ef-85df-0ae687ad910c" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380195 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380195 1111 #uuid "43c20240-428f-5295-ac13-745401af8941" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380196 1034 "2" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380196 1111 #uuid "b39fbfd4-ff69-5b93-9537-86630db7fb44" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380197 1034 "-3" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380197 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380197 1111 #uuid "5b1511a1-0592-5e16-ae3d-355dbe352c92" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380198 1034 "-2" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380198 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380198 1111 #uuid "aed5ce7a-ce77-563e-a120-802fb7c3c0e8" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380199 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380200 13194139536033 true] [17592186380199 1089 "q-127910" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380199 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536033 true] [17592186380199 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380199 1113 #uuid "05136695-9e80-59ef-a336-fc6a855ca97f" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380199 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & ={t}_{2}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨3,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=3.$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380201 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380202 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380203 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380204 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380205 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1041 "selection" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380201 13194139536033 true] [17592186380200 1110 #uuid "eafa7ebb-6b96-5c3c-a7ed-5307588cc416" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380201 1034 "3" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380201 1111 #uuid "89f6d816-5381-5306-b4c9-c34c049885d0" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380202 1034 "\\sqrt{7}" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380202 1111 #uuid "331a3a0d-e903-59b3-9147-23a3def27b44" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380203 1034 "1" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380203 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380203 1111 #uuid "41eae54d-3456-5113-9d8b-1c7ace24b718" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380204 1034 "-3" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380204 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380204 1111 #uuid "a7e21bff-5775-520e-aa3f-3af78aec6c30" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380205 1034 "-1" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380205 1111 #uuid "be7da4de-0848-51fe-be88-efe52ae6412b" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380206 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380207 13194139536033 true] [17592186380206 1089 "q-127927" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380206 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536033 true] [17592186380206 1100 "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1).$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380206 1113 #uuid "5fb6c451-3fd1-5933-bfd5-1dcab52c2777" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380206 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,-3,1⟩-⟨4,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨3,-4,4⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =⟨1,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380208 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380209 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380210 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380211 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380212 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1041 "selection" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380212 13194139536033 true] [17592186380207 1110 #uuid "4ea1771e-337a-53ba-af67-134749c7dc53" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380208 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,4⟩=11" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380208 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380208 1111 #uuid "06b379fd-7d70-5e49-8081-a3b64f84134e" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380209 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨-4,-4,3⟩=11" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380209 1111 #uuid "0d2c1c27-eb96-5b3b-9be4-85fc3ed5d870" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380210 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨3,4,4⟩=23" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380210 1111 #uuid "18790217-0164-5be5-8309-2e02c079a999" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380211 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,4⟩=12" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380211 1111 #uuid "56439333-b485-5577-b3fc-2b0a4fb30508" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380212 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380212 1111 #uuid "0677a85c-be73-579f-a4cd-3b2a328033da" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380214 13194139536033 true] [17592186380213 1089 "q-127948" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536033 true] [17592186380213 1100 "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380213 1113 #uuid "0063bd61-9495-5b7f-ae6d-384a92c58a15" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380213 1145 "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,2,1⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,-2⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨6,-5,4⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380215 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380216 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380217 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380218 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380219 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1041 "selection" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380218 13194139536033 true] [17592186380214 1110 #uuid "8c8d44ee-444f-5365-a1c8-4d6392e75dfb" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380215 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨-6,4,5⟩=28" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380215 1111 #uuid "24d09d6d-587a-5131-bf7b-17c4a5299f8c" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380216 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨6,5,-4⟩=24" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380216 1111 #uuid "97b1a154-e6ea-5ad5-bc67-985ac790249f" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380217 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨4,-5,6⟩=-28" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380217 1111 #uuid "c19bf435-7bb8-561f-ba12-0c791dd434be" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380218 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380218 1111 #uuid "6397ae12-fbfa-5ef2-932b-49e1d8b15ea1" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380219 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨-5,6,4⟩=12" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380219 1111 #uuid "facf8c4b-8e3d-5a24-a63e-b12fc172190e" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380220 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380221 13194139536033 true] [17592186380220 1089 "q-70895" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380220 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536033 true] [17592186380220 1100 "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(3,-5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380220 1113 #uuid "ca2b2271-1ec0-5a3e-b5ac-687d91668797" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380220 1145 "Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-5,-2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=4-t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨2,3,4⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-3,4,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩ & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380222 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380223 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380224 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380225 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380226 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1041 "selection" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380226 13194139536033 true] [17592186380221 1110 #uuid "b6b8fc01-b722-5332-8a4b-09309993af92" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380222 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨3,-5,-2⟩=⟨-3,4,-1⟩" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 true] [17592186380222 1111 #uuid "4ed6607f-2a3f-5645-9a9a-7de309608bb4" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380223 1034 "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,-1⟩=⟨3,-5,-2⟩" 13194139536033 true] [17592186380223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536033 t